        "original_id": "fad7fe02-b644-5b43-a873-5693e5bc00e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Albany County, Colonie, Latham, Boght Corners, Troy, New York\n- Roads: New York State Route 9R, New York State Route 470, U.S. Route 9, U.S. Route 4\n\nFacts:\n- New York State Route 9R is a north–south state highway in northeastern Albany County, New York.\n- New York State Route 9R leaves U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Latham and rejoins U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Boght Corners, and both hamlets are in the town of Colonie.\n- Boght Corners, also called Boght, is a hamlet in the town of Colonie in northern Albany County, New York, and it straddles U.S. Route 9.\n- New York State Route 470 extends 2.91 miles from an intersection with New York State Route 9R in the town of Colonie to a junction with U.S. Route 4 in the city of Troy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "79c51dcf-4de8-58bd-86c3-0684b0f63ea2",
        "text": "Page: New York State Route 9R. Sentence: New York State Route 9R (NY 9R) is a north–south state highway in northeastern Albany County, New York, in the United States.\nPage: New York State Route 9R. Sentence: It leaves US 9 in the hamlet of Latham and rejoins its parent in the hamlet of Boght Corners, both located in the town of Colonie.\nPage: Boght Corners, New York. Sentence: Boght Corners (also referred to as Boght) is a hamlet in the town of Colonie in northern Albany County, New York that straddles U.S. Route 9 (Route 9).\nPage: New York State Route 470. Sentence: It extends for 2.91 mi from an intersection with NY 9R in the town of Colonie to a junction with U.S. Route 4 (US 4) in the city of Troy.",
